  "node": {
    "id": "ctkg:v3e-object-f4d8dd28d3b00dca6664a0ec",
    "canonicalType": "KnowledgeStatement",
    "label": "当设计指标包含误差常数要求时，伯德图法更为适用，因为在 s 平面上设计的系统，其误差常数必须在选定补偿器的极点和零点之后才能确定。因此，当指定误差常数时，根轨迹法通常会导致迭代设计过程。另一方面，当指标以超调量百分比和调节时间给出，从而确定了 s 平面上期望主导根的 zeta 和 omega_n 时，根轨迹法是一种非常令人满意的方法。",
    "aliases": [],
    "description": "When the design specifications include an error constant requirement, the Bode plot method is more suitable, because the error constant of a system designed on the s-plane must be ascertained following the choice of a compensator pole and zero. Therefore, the root locus method often results in an iterative design procedure when the error constant is specified. On the other hand, the root locus is a very satisfactory approach when the specifications are given in terms of percent overshoot and settling time, thus specifying the zeta and omega_n of the desired dominant roots in the s-plane.",
